.TH MCP-TERMINAL-PREFLIGHT 1 "@VERSION@" "mcp-terminal-docker" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mcp-terminal-preflight \- validate MCP Terminal configuration and runtime prerequisites
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mcp-terminal-preflight
.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs the same validation chain as service startup:
.PP
.RS
.IP 1.
Placeholder resolution (\fBCHANGE_ME\fR, \fBWATCH_DIRS_ROOT\fR, etc.)
.IP 2.
JSON schema and cross-field rules (\fBconfig_validator\fR)
.IP 3.
Runtime preflight: TLS files readable, \fBwatch_dirs\fR visibility and write access,
\fB/var/mcp-terminal\fR writable, Docker socket and CLI API version,
\fBcode_analysis.ssl.ca\fR sanity, SSH host-execution prerequisites when
\fBterminal_host_exec\fR is enabled (\fBssh.known_hosts_path\fR, key manager script).
.RE
.PP
When the \fBmcp-terminal\fR container is running, validation executes inside the
container (same uid, groups, and bind mounts as production). Otherwise a host-side
check runs with Docker checks skipped.
.PP
On service start, all findings are written to the application log
(\fB/var/log/mcp-terminal/\fR): errors prevent startup; warnings are logged but
do not block startup.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Configuration passes schema and runtime error checks (warnings may still print).
.TP
.B 1
Validation failed (missing files, permissions, unresolved placeholders, etc.).
.SH EXAMPLES
Validate before recreate:
.PP
.RS
.EX
sudo mcp-terminal-docker recreate
mcp-terminal-preflight
.EE
.RE
.PP
Validate from inside a dev venv:
.PP
.RS
.EX
python3 -m mcp_terminal.config.config_cli validate \\
  -c /etc/mcp-terminal/term_server.json
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mcp-terminal-config (5),
.BR mcp-terminal-docker (1),
.BR info (1) \fBmcp-terminal-docker\fR
